---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const article = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: 'Australia Visitor Visa (600) from Pakistan — Complete Guide',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'VisaPath.pk' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'VisaPath.pk' },
  datePublished: '2026-10-24',
};

const faq = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    { '@type': 'Question', name: 'How much does Australia visitor visa cost from Pakistan?',
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'The Subclass 600 Visitor Visa base application fee is AUD $190 (approximately PKR 35,000). Family of applicants attracts additional charges.' } },
    { '@type': 'Question', name: 'How long does Australia visitor visa take?',
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Processing time for Subclass 600 from Pakistan typically ranges from 4–12 weeks, varying by applicant profile and application completeness.' } },
    { '@type': 'Question', name: 'Can I convert visitor visa to work visa in Australia?',
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Visitor visas usually have a "No Further Stay" condition (8503), preventing you from applying for most other visas while in Australia.' } },
  ],
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Australia Visitor Visa (600) from Pakistan — Complete Guide"
  description="Pakistani guide to Australia Subclass 600 visitor visa. Tourist stream, business visitor, sponsored family, requirements, processing times."
  schema={[article, faq]}
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
    <nav class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Home</a> ›
      <a href="/guides/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Guides</a> ›
      <span>Australia Visitor Visa</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Australia Visitor Visa (600) from Pakistan — Complete Guide</h1>
    <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm mb-8">Last updated: October 2026 · 9 minute read</p>

    <section class="prose max-w-none">
      <p class="lead text-lg">
        Australia's Subclass 600 Visitor Visa is the standard route for Pakistani travelers visiting Australia for tourism, business meetings, or family. This guide covers the four streams, requirements, and how to maximize approval chances.
      </p>

      <h2>Four Streams of Subclass 600</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Tourist Stream:</strong> for tourism, visiting family and friends, short cruises</li>
        <li><strong>Business Visitor Stream:</strong> business meetings, conferences, contract negotiations</li>
        <li><strong>Sponsored Family Stream:</strong> family in Australia sponsors your visit, security bond may apply</li>
        <li><strong>Approved Destination Status (ADS):</strong> for Chinese tour groups, not applicable to Pakistanis</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Most Pakistani applicants use either Tourist Stream (visiting family/holidays) or Business Visitor Stream (work-related).
      </p>

      <h2>Visa Duration</h2>
      <p>
        If approved, Subclass 600 typically grants:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>3, 6, or 12 months</strong> stay per entry</li>
        <li><strong>Single or multiple entry</strong> depending on application</li>
        <li><strong>Up to 3 years validity</strong> for frequent visitors with good travel history</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Costs</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Visa Application Charge:</strong> AUD $190 (approximately PKR 35,000)</li>
        <li><strong>Additional applicant charges</strong> for dependents on the same application</li>
        <li><strong>Biometrics (where required):</strong> handled by VFS Global in Pakistan</li>
        <li><strong>Health examinations:</strong> may be required (AUD $400–$600 per person)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Documents Required</h2>
      <h3>Core Documents</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Current passport + all previous passports</li>
        <li>Recent photographs</li>
        <li>CNIC + Family Registration Certificate (FRC)</li>
        <li>Marriage certificate / children's birth certificates (if applicable)</li>
        <li>Completed online application via ImmiAccount</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Financial Evidence</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Bank statements — 6 months, personal account</li>
        <li>Salary slips or business income proof</li>
        <li>Tax returns</li>
        <li>Property ownership documents</li>
        <li>Fixed deposits (if applicable)</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Employment / Business</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Employment letter stating position, salary, approved leave, return confirmation</li>
        <li>Business registration documents (if self-employed)</li>
        <li>Letter from client/organizer (if business travel)</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Travel Plans</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Flight bookings (reservation acceptable, not required to be purchased)</li>
        <li>Hotel bookings or address of accommodation</li>
        <li>Day-by-day itinerary</li>
        <li>Travel insurance (recommended)</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>If Visiting Family/Friends</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Letter of invitation from Australian host</li>
        <li>Host's visa/citizenship proof</li>
        <li>Host's financial documents (if sponsoring)</li>
        <li>Family relationship evidence (if visiting relatives)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Application Process</h2>
      <h3>Step 1 — Create ImmiAccount</h3>
      <p>
        Register at <code>online.immi.gov.au</code> — official Australian immigration portal.
      </p>

      <h3>Step 2 — Complete Online Application</h3>
      <p>
        Fill out all sections carefully. Upload supporting documents (PDF format, each file under 5MB).
      </p>

      <h3>Step 3 — Pay the Fee</h3>
      <p>
        Credit card payment within ImmiAccount. Receipt generated automatically.
      </p>

      <h3>Step 4 — Submit Biometrics</h3>
      <p>
        After submission, you receive a biometrics instruction letter. Book an appointment at VFS Global Australia Visa Application Centre in Islamabad, Lahore, or Karachi within 14 days.
      </p>

      <h3>Step 5 — Health Examination (if required)</h3>
      <p>
        You may be asked to undergo a health check at an approved panel physician. Required for:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Visits over 6 months</li>
        <li>Applicants with certain health conditions</li>
        <li>Visitors going to Australian healthcare, childcare, or education settings</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Step 6 — Decision</h3>
      <p>
        Decision communicated via ImmiAccount email. If approved, visa grant letter issued electronically — no stamp in passport. You carry the grant letter and show it at airline check-in and Australian immigration.
      </p>

      <h2>Common Refusal Reasons</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Weak ties to Pakistan</strong> — officer not convinced you'll return</li>
        <li><strong>Insufficient funds</strong> — unable to support stay comfortably</li>
        <li><strong>Vague travel purpose</strong> — unclear itinerary or inconsistent plans</li>
        <li><strong>Immigration risk indicators</strong> — single, young, no property or employment</li>
        <li><strong>Previous overstays or refusals</strong> in Australia or other countries</li>
        <li><strong>Document inconsistencies</strong> — different information across sources</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Section 8503 — No Further Stay Condition</h2>
      <p>
        Most Pakistani visitor visas are issued with Condition 8503 attached. This means:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>You cannot apply for most other visas while in Australia</li>
        <li>You must leave Australia and apply for any new visa from outside</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Removal of 8503 is possible in exceptional circumstances but rarely granted.
      </p>

      <h2>Travel Tips for Pakistani Visitors</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Major cities to visit:</strong> Sydney, Melbourne, Brisbane, Perth</li>
        <li><strong>Flights:</strong> Via Dubai, Doha, Singapore, or Kuala Lumpur</li>
        <li><strong>Flight time:</strong> 15–20 hours from Pakistan with 1 connection</li>
        <li><strong>Season:</strong> Australian summer (Dec–Feb), winter (Jun–Aug) — opposite of Pakistan</li>
        <li><strong>Visa documentation:</strong> keep digital and printed grant letter</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Super Visa Alternative — Parent Visitor Visa (Subclass 870)</h2>
      <p>
        Parents of Australian citizens or PRs can apply for Subclass 870 (Sponsored Parent) — up to 5 years stay without needing to leave. Expensive but valuable for long family visits.
      </p>

      <h2>Related Resources</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="/tools/visa-fee-calculator/">Fee Calculator</a> ·
        <a href="/tools/document-checklist-generator/">Document Checklist</a> ·
        <a href="/tools/visa-interview-questions/">Interview Questions</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
